  "id": "mixed-receptive-expressive-language-disorder",
  "term": "mixed receptive-expressive language disorder",
  "definition": "A disorder in which both understanding language and expressing language are impaired, despite nonverbal intellectual abilities being relatively stronger. It may arise during development or be acquired after brain injury such as a lesion or head trauma.",
